 the @HA, @HK, or @CA - they are quick losers - the opponents can take them whenever they gain the lead. "],["pg",""],["lc","hakca"],["hs","ss"],["at","Plan, therefore, to eliminate your Spade loser. "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["hs","nh"],["at","You can't trump it in dummy and don't have any immediate sure tricks on which to discard it. "],["pg",""],["ls","nh"],["hs","nc"],["at","However, you can establish an extra Club winner in dummy "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["hc","ca"],["at","by driving out the opponents' @CA."],["pg",""],["lc","ca"],["hs","ss"],["nt","\nAfter winning the first trick, can you start drawing trump? "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["pc","s"],["pc","s"],["pc","sa"],["pg",""],["hs","nc"],["at","To establish the extra Club winner, you must give up the lead to the opponents. "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["hs","ss"],["at","You can afford to do this once; because your Spade loser is slow, they can't immediately take a Spade trick. "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["hs","sh"],["nt","\nTo draw trump you must also give up the lead to the opponents. If you do so "],["pg",""],["ls","sh"],["pc","hq"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["hs","ws"],["at","the opponents may lead another Spade. "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["pc","sj"],["pc","sk"],["pc","s"],["pc","s"],["pg",""],["hs","ss"],["hs","ns"],["at","You will have no high cards left in Spades "],["pg",""],["ls","ns"],["at","and your remaining Spade is a quick loser. "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["hs","nc"],["at","You can't discard it because you have not yet established the extra Club winner in dummy, and you can't establish the extra winner without giving up the lead again."],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["up","11"],["hc","sa"],["nt","\nSince you will have to let the opponents in when you draw trump, you cannot afford to draw trump right away on this deal. You must carefully win the first Spade trick with the @SA, "],["pg",""],["lc","sa"],["pc","s"],["pc","s"],["pc","sa"],["pg",""],["hc","sk"],["at","making sure to preserve the @SK as an entry to the dummy."],["pg",""],["lc","sk"],["hc","cj"],["nt","Next you lead the @CJ, high card from the short side, "],["pg",""],["lc","cj"],["pc","cj"],["pc","c"],["pc","c"],["hs","nc"],["at","to start to establish the extra Club winner. "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["hc","ca"],["at","If the opponents do not play their @CA, "],["pg",""],["lc","ca"],["pc","c"],["pg",""],["hs","sc"],["at","lead the suit again "],["pg",""],["ls","sc"],["pc","c"],["pc","c"],["pc","ck"],["hs","ec"],["at","to drive it out. "],["pg",""],["ls","ec"],["pc","ca"],["pg",""],["hs","es"],["at","When they lead back a Spade, "],["pg",""],["ls","es"],["pc","s"],["pc","s"],["pc","s"],["hc","sk"],["at","win it in dummy with your carefully preserved @SK, "],["pg",""],["lc","sk"],["pc","sk"],["pg",""],["hs","nc"],["at","then play your established Club winner "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["pc","c"],["pc","c"],["hs","ss"],["at","and discard a Spade on it. "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["pc","s"],["pc","c"],["pg",""],["at","Now it is safe to start drawing the opponents' trump because you have only three losers."],["",""]]}}